indicator("Lipi Probe", overlay=true)

// Throwaway diagnostic, not a study. Paste it into the Lipi Editor and press
// Save. It marks every up bar and every bar with volume, so if it renders at
// all you know plotting works and both constructs below are accepted.
//
// It exists to settle two things the GoCharting docs describe but that no
// compile in this repo has ever confirmed:
//   SECTION 1  plotshape's `text` parameter
//   SECTION 2  the `volume` built-in
//   SECTION 3  the `dayofweek` built-in (needed for previous-week levels)
//
// HOW TO READ THE RESULT
//   Saves, and triangles appear      both constructs work
//   Fails -> delete SECTION 2 -> saves    `volume` is the problem
//   Fails -> delete `text=` args -> saves `text` is the problem
//   Fails -> delete SECTION 3 -> saves    `dayofweek` is the problem
//   Fails with all three removed     something else - send me the error text
//
// Whichever one fails, the fix in the real scripts is to delete that construct:
// every text= argument, or the RVOL / VWAP blocks that use volume.

// ==== SECTION 1: plotshape text parameter ====
upBar = close > open
plotshape(upBar, shape=shape.triangleup, location=location.belowbar, color=color.green, size=size.small, text="UP", title="Text Probe")

// ==== SECTION 2: volume built-in ====
zeroF = high - high
hasVol = volume > zeroF
plotshape(hasVol, shape=shape.triangledown, location=location.abovebar, color=color.orange, size=size.small, text="V", title="Volume Probe")

// ==== SECTION 3: dayofweek built-in ====
newWeek = dayofweek < dayofweek[1]
plotshape(newWeek, shape=shape.triangleup, location=location.abovebar, color=color.purple, size=size.small, text="W", title="Dayofweek Probe")
